  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_susuro",
      "name": {
        "en": "Sussurro's Badge",
        "zh": "苏苏洛证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_susuro",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Sussurro has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for healing teammates in the field.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Medic Operator during field operations to exercise Medic responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员苏苏洛擅长在战场上为干员提供治疗\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为医疗干员，行使医师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_susuro",
      "name": {
        "en": "...Who Heals Not Herself",
        "zh": "医不自治",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_susuro",
      "description": {
        "en": "Based on my grasp of the situation, the Originium crystals present on the Infected by all rights shouldn't be active. The professor and student mentors haven't shown any symptoms—which is to say, ordinary contact with an Infected, and even treatment of them, likely doesn't lead to infection at all.\nWhich lets me confirm that I was only infected because I made contact with Originium while it was in an active state.\nAs for the active Originium's origins: Was this region already polluted by Originium?—Unlikely, because the professor and student mentors weren't infected. Was it my contact with Infected blood?—Not impossible.\nI can be sure that Infected blood carries traces of active Originium. If so, I need to distinguish whether the areas I contacted at the time were open wounds, how long the contact lasted, the freshness of contacted blood, etc. For all factors.\nIf there was a wound, fresh blood was contacted, and contact was prolonged, I can hypothesize resultant infection was inevitable; if there was a wound, stale blood was contacted, and contact was brief, would infection occur? This can determine whether or not Originium activity in the blood of Infected wanes as time passes. Also, if there was no wound and fresh blood was contacted; if there was no wound, stale blood was contacted...\nUnfortunately, I don't remember the exact circumstances. Actually, I don't even know how I was infected. I was too busy...\nBut I do remember that before I discovered Originium crystals on my body, I had a fever, headaches, and other symptoms. Right, I was under the impression for a few days that I'd fallen ill from overwork. Now I see it must have been a sort of initial onset of the Oripathy infection. I often hear patients give similar accounts of their own circumstances during diagnosis.\nPlus, given a view informed by the critical care of Infected over the past days, my own condition is relatively mild, but I can't be sure of anything without further tests.\nThat's the best summary I can give for now. If I think of anything else later, I'll add it here.\nThe professor and mentors are staying here to continue their assignments. Aside from providing some practical accounts of Infected life from the perspective of a doctor, I'm not much help anymore. I'm currently searching for a medical organization that specializes in researching and treating Oripathy. As volunteers in the face of this still-unknown disease, we can't provide very effective care to those who need it most, and there may even be further infections down the line. We need more specialized, in-depth research before we can confront this sickness.\nWould such an organization exist?\n—Sussurro's diary entry following Oripathy diagnosis",
        "zh": "根据我目前掌握的情况来看，感染者身上的源石结晶应该并非活性源石。因为老师和前辈们并没有出现任何感染的症状——也就是说，正常地接触感染者，甚至是医治他们，可能并不会导致感染。\n那么现在可以确认的是，我是因为接触了活性状态下的源石才导致的感染。\n活性源石的来源，是这片区域已经被源石污染？——可能性不大，因为老师和前辈们并没有感染。是我接触了感染者的血液？——有一定可能。\n能够确定的是感染者体内的血液带有活性源石成分。这样的话，还要分我接触时接触的部分是否带有伤口、接触时间长短、接触的血液新鲜程度等各种情况。\n如果有伤口，接触了新鲜血液，且接触时间较长，我推测必然导致感染；如果有伤口，接触了放置一段时间的血液，较长时间地接触会感染吗？这能确认感染者血液中的源石活性是否会根据时间的增长而消失。还有没有伤口，接触了新鲜血液；没有伤口，接触放置了一段时间的血液……\n可惜，我并不记得当时的情况了。甚至，我其实不知道自己是怎么感染的，太忙了……\n但我记得，我在发现自己体表的源石结晶前，出现了发烧、头晕等症状。对，那几天我还以为自己太过疲劳才生病的，现在看来，这应该就是感染矿石病的一种初期表现。我在诊治时也经常听到患者这么描述自己的情况。\n以及，根据这段日子救治的感染者来看，我的病症算是轻症，但在做进一步检测之前，这些还都不能确认。\n目前能总结的就是这些，以后再有什么想到的我再补充到这里。\n老师和前辈们还要留在这里继续他们的任务，我除了以一个医生的角度提供一些感染者的切实感受以外，已经帮不上什么忙了。我正在试图寻找一些专门收治和研究矿石病的医疗机构，对于这种尚且未知的疾病，仅靠我们这些志愿者并不能起到非常良好的救治效果，甚至可能会出现像我这样反而被感染的情况，我们需要更专业和更深入的研究，才能对抗这种疾病。\n会有这样的机构吗？\n——苏苏洛在确诊矿石病后的日记",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
